Text: The results are shown in Figure 4. It can be seen that both the encoder and decoder are more sensitive to noun (NN) and adjective (JJ). How- ever, compared with the encoder, the decoder is less sensitive to preposition (IN), determiner (DT), pronoun (PRP), adverb (RB), verb (VB) and coor- dinating conjunction (CC) but much more sensi- tive to EOS, which is used to determine the end of a sentence.

